    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 25-layer SiO2/Al2O3 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layers 0-12 alternate SiO2/Al2O3 starting with SiO2. Layers 13-17 are fixed at thicknesses [70.0, 51.0, 61.0, 47.0, 61.0] nm with materials [SiO2, Al2O3, SiO2, Al2O3, SiO2]. Layers 18-24 alternate Al2O3/SiO2 ending with SiO2. Optimize thicknesses of layers 0-12 and 18-24 with bounds ±20% from quarter-wave optical thickness at 267.5nm center wavelength. Score candidates by mean transmittance in 255-280nm (maximize), 300-700nm (minimize), and 700-1100nm (minimize). Use coherent TMM solver across 255-1100nm spectrum. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 255–280 nm; low transmittance in 300–700 nm; low transmittance in 700–1100 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 300–700 nm; transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30; no metal layers; conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials only.",
